---
import { BellOff, Camera, ShieldAlert } from "@lucide/astro";
import RedditPixel from "../components/RedditPixel.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeaderV7.astro";
import SiteMediaLoader from "../components/SiteMediaLoader.astro";
import "../styles/global-v7.css";
import "../styles/about-harbor.css";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <RedditPixel />
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="robots" content="index,follow" />
    <title>About Harbor Innovations | HarborNavi</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Why Harbor Innovations is building HarborNavi: a private, local memory and intelligence layer for the home." />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.png" type="image/png" sizes="512x512" data-media-slot="site-favicon" />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://harbornavi.com/about-harbor" />
  </head>
  <body class="about-page" data-route="about-harbor">
    <SiteHeader ctaHref="/pilot-families#apply" homeHref="/home-v9" />
    <main>
      <section class="about-hero" aria-labelledby="about-title">
        <img src="/assets/home-v7-v8-memory-hero-id.webp" alt="A family sharing an everyday moment at home while HarborNavi keeps selected memories local" width="1536" height="1024" fetchpriority="high" data-media-slot="about-hero" />
        <div class="about-hero-shade"></div>
        <div class="about-hero-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">Local intelligence for the place that matters most</p>
          <h1 id="about-title">Harbor Innovations</h1>
          <p class="about-hero-line">Why we left Big Tech to build a memory for the home.</p>
          <a href="#founding-story">Read our story <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="founding-story" class="about-story section-shell" aria-labelledby="story-title">
        <div class="about-section-label"><span>01</span><p>Founding story</p></div>
        <div class="about-story-copy">
          <h2 id="story-title">Our homes kept recording. They still forgot us.</h2>
          <p>An important family moment could be captured, then buried in a full day of footage. A smart speaker could know tomorrow's schedule, yet anyone nearby could ask. A package could disappear before an alert became useful.</p>
          <div class="about-story-scenarios" aria-label="Examples of home technology missing privacy and context">
            <figure class="about-story-scenario">
              <div class="about-story-visual">
                <img src="/assets/about-story-speaker-privacy-v1.jpg" alt="An unfamiliar visitor asking a smart speaker about the homeowner's schedule while the home is empty" width="1536" height="1024" loading="lazy" data-media-slot="about-story-speaker-privacy" />
                <div class="story-dialogue story-dialogue-question"><span>Visitor</span><p>What time will Alex be out tomorrow?</p></div>
                <div class="story-dialogue story-dialogue-answer"><span>Smart speaker</span><p>Alex leaves at 8:15 AM.</p></div>
                <div class="story-risk-status"><ShieldAlert size={16} strokeWidth={1.9} aria-hidden="true" /><span>No identity check</span></div>
              </div>
              <figcaption><strong>It knew the schedule, not who was asking.</strong><span>Anyone nearby could ask for private household context.</span></figcaption>
            </figure>
            <figure class="about-story-scenario">
              <div class="about-story-visual">
                <img src="/assets/about-story-package-recorded-v1.jpg" alt="A porch camera recording a stranger opening a delivered package without sending a useful alert" width="1536" height="1024" loading="lazy" data-media-slot="about-story-package-recorded" />
                <div class="story-camera-status"><Camera size={15} strokeWidth={1.9} aria-hidden="true" /><span>Porch camera</span><b>Recording</b></div>
                <div class="story-missed-alert"><BellOff size={18} strokeWidth={1.9} aria-hidden="true" /><span><small>Package activity detected</small>Recorded. No alert sent.</span></div>
              </div>
              <figcaption><strong>It captured the theft, but did not help in time.</strong><span>A useful home should recognize the situation and notify the owner while action is still possible.</span></figcaption>
            </figure>
          </div>
          <p>Something was broken about how homes remember. The signals existed, but context, privacy, and action lived in separate systems. We decided to build the missing layer ourselves.</p>
          <blockquote>Home technology should remember for the family, not learn from the family for someone else.</blockquote>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="about-beliefs" aria-labelledby="beliefs-title">
        <div class="section-shell">
          <div class="about-section-label"><span>02</span><p>What we believe</p></div>
          <h2 id="beliefs-title">Two principles guide every product decision.</h2>
          <div class="belief-lines">
            <p><span aria-hidden="true">01</span>A home memory should last a lifetime.</p>
            <p><span aria-hidden="true">02</span>Privacy is not a premium feature.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="about-projects section-shell" aria-labelledby="projects-title">
        <div class="about-section-label"><span>03</span><p>What we built before</p></div>
        <div class="about-projects-heading">
          <h2 id="projects-title">HarborNavi grows from years of local AI work.</h2>
          <p>Hardware, operating systems, and real workflows taught us that local intelligence must be capable, understandable, and easy to live with.</p>
        </div>
        <article class="project-row">
          <figure><img src="/assets/about-nexus-workstation-v1.jpg" alt="The Nexus AI Workstation installed in a warm home workspace" width="1398" height="786" loading="lazy" data-media-slot="about-nexus" /></figure>
          <div><span>Project 01</span><h3>Nexus AI Workstation</h3><p>Our local AI hardware foundation: dedicated compute, upgradeable storage, and practical on-device workflows.</p></div>
        </article>
        <article class="project-row project-row-reverse">
          <figure><img src="/assets/home-v7-v8-hardware-id.webp" alt="HarborNavi hardware with a forged-carbon-fiber top running the local Harbor OS intelligence layer" width="1536" height="1024" loading="lazy" data-media-slot="about-harbor-os" /></figure>
          <div><span>Project 02</span><h3>Harbor OS</h3><p>The software layer that brings local models, devices, permissions, and explainable actions into one system.</p></div>
        </article>
      </section>

      <section class="about-voices" aria-labelledby="voices-title">
        <div class="section-shell about-voices-grid">
          <div>
            <div class="about-section-label"><span>04</span><p>Advisors, backers & early voices</p></div>
            <h2 id="voices-title">Built with people who challenge the details.</h2>
            <p>We are working with product builders, smart-home experts, and early families. Names and formal endorsements will be published only with permission.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="voice-themes" aria-label="Themes from early product feedback">
            <p><span>01</span>Local-first should feel simpler, not more technical.</p>
            <p><span>02</span>Interoperability matters more than another closed ecosystem.</p>
            <p><span>03</span>Family memory must stay owner-controlled.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="about-now section-shell" aria-labelledby="now-title">
        <div class="about-section-label"><span>05</span><p>Why now</p></div>
        <div class="about-now-heading">
          <h2 id="now-title">Three things changed.</h2>
          <p>The technology became ready just as families began demanding a better privacy model.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="now-grid">
          <article><span>01</span><h3>Edge AI became capable</h3><p>60 TOPS-class hardware can run meaningful models where the data lives.</p></article>
          <article><span>02</span><h3>Device interoperability matured</h3><p>Home Assistant made a broad, local device layer practical.</p></article>
          <article><span>03</span><h3>People started asking who listens</h3><p>Convenience no longer excuses sending a home's full history away.</p></article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="about-cta" aria-labelledby="about-cta-title">
        <div class="section-shell">
          <p class="eyebrow">Five homes. One honest first step.</p>
          <h2 id="about-cta-title">Help us get HarborNavi right.</h2>
          <p>We're looking for five families. If our story resonates, we'd love to hear yours.</p>
          <a class="about-primary" href="/pilot-families#apply">Apply to Join the Pilot <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>
    <footer class="site-footer"><span>HarborNavi</span><a href="/home-v9">Home</a><a href="/pilot-families">Pilot Program</a><a href="/privacy">Privacy</a></footer>
    <SiteMediaLoader />
  </body>
</html>
